module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.adjacent_passive_accelerators_starve_each_other

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, MechanicallyPreventable }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

// A PASSIVE ACCELERATOR PLACED WHERE ITS SLOT'S GEOMETRY AND AIRFLOW DO NOT COOL IT. The invalid state
// is not adjacency: it is a placement whose per-slot geometry (pitch, clearance to the neighbouring
// card's envelope, the card's own slot width) together with the airflow that reaches that position
// leaves the card below the cooling its rating assumes, which shows as thermal slowdown, minimum
// clocks or a GPU leaving the bus. On the H11 that placement was two A16 boards in adjacent slots, so
// adjacency was the configuration the incident happened in, not the rule it proves: another chassis
// with a different slot pitch or airflow can carry two passive cards side by side, and refusing every
// adjacent pair would forbid more than the evidence supports (operator ruling, 2026-10-30, cited in
// evidence below). The authority is per-slot geometry and airflow plus the measured thermal behaviour
// of the installed position; the name keeps the identity the incident was filed under.

data adjacent_passive_accelerators_starve_each_other: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "adjacent_passive_accelerators_starve_each_other" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, ceiling: MechanicallyPreventable, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "each host's per-slot geometry (physical order, pitch, clearance to the neighbouring envelope) and the airflow reaching each GPU position are modelled, and the gpu card host program's measurement instrument reads each installed position under load as a required input to seat admission, so a position whose reading shows thermal slowdown, minimum clocks or bus loss refuses admission while an adjacent pair whose slots and airflow hold it is admitted on its reading" } },

  receipts: [
    "THE INCIDENT, AS EVIDENCE FOR THAT CONFIGURATION: on the H11 host, two NVIDIA A16 boards in adjacent x16-capable slots reached 96 to 99 C under load even at minimum clocks, and one GPU dropped off the PCIe bus. Read by the operator session holding the host, 2026-10-25. It establishes that this slot pitch with this chassis airflow does not cool two adjacent A16 boards; it does not establish that adjacency fails on every host.",

    "THE MITIGATION THAT WORKED, BY HAND: moving the boards to SLOT2 and SLOT6, with a slot between them, removed the outright failure (48 to 81 C at idle and partial load). That move was an operator judgement with no model behind it, which is what keeps the class at mitigatable. Even spaced, the first GPU of each board reached 87 to 88 C with SW thermal slowdown at full load, so heat depends on GPU position within a board and spacing alone is not the authority.",

    "WHAT THE BOARD ALREADY SAYS: extdeps.boards.supermicro_h11ssl supermicro_h11ssl_pcie_slots lists the slots and their lane counts but not their physical order or pitch, so neither adjacency nor clearance is derivable from the model today. Lane count alone would have admitted the failing placement: both slots were x16.",

    "THE SCOPE, BY OPERATOR RULING (2026-10-30, relayed by keen-otter-392 from calm-moth-166 and proud-raven): adjacent passive cards are not refused as a class. Slot spacing differs between chassis (Butch's is not the H11's), so admission is judged per slot from geometry and airflow plus the measured thermal behaviour of the installed position.",

    "THE CEILING: mechanically preventable. Geometry is decidable from upstream and catalog facts, but whether a position is cooled depends on airflow and the measured behaviour of the card in it, so the class is caught by the measurement gating seat admission rather than made unwritable by construction. The residual, a zone whose fans do not follow the card at all, is the class a_passive_accelerator_sits_in_a_zone_that_does_not_follow_it.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.design_ruling", decl_name: "passive_card_adjacency_is_judged_per_slot_and_by_measurement", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
